    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336-a1">

                <pb facs="0841" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg801"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Agenda for US-UK Oil Talks on April</hi> 5,
                    1954</head>
                <list>
                    <label>I.</label>
                    <item>Pipeline transit agreements in the Middle East.</item>
                    <label>II.</label>
                    <item>Saudi Arabia. <list>
                            <label>a.</label>
                            <item>Status of Aramco-SAG negotiations</item>
                            <label>b.</label>
                            <item>Status of Onassis tanker deal</item>
                            <label>c.</label>
                            <item>Implications of boundary questions for international oil
                                development.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>III.</label>
                    <item>Reexamination of attitudes toward 50–50 oil concession agreements.</item>
                    <label>IV.</label>
                    <item>Implications for other Middle East production of reentry of Iranian oil
                        into world markets.</item>
                    <label>V.</label>
                    <item>Oil company-government relations in the Middle East.</item>
                    <label>VI.</label>
                    <item>Relation of antitrust questions to Middle East oil problems.</item>
                    <label>VII.</label>
                    <item>Should there be periodic US–UK–Dutch–French oil talks?</item>
                    <label>VIII.</label>
                    <item>General economic and political trends (e.g., nationalism) in the Middle
                        East and their significance for petroleum operations in the area.</item>
                    <label>IX.</label>
                    <item>Soviet oil. <list>
                            <label>a.</label>
                            <item>Soviet objectives in expanding sales</item>
                            <label>b.</label>
                            <item>US–UK Government position on question of their nationals being
                                forced by local governments to handle and/or market Soviet
                                oil</item>
                            <label>c.</label>
                            <item>Security aspects, if any, to West of expanding Soviet oil
                                sales.</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
